# Copy this file to .env in this folder (backend/.env, next to manage.py), then
# fill in what you need. .env is git-ignored, so passwords stay off GitHub.
# - One NAME=value per line, with nothing else on the line (no comments after it).
# - Save it as UTF-8. VS Code does this by default. Don't create it with
#   PowerShell's echo, which saves UTF-16.
# - Restart the server after changing it.

# ---- Email (optional) --------------------------------------------------------
# Without these two lines, emails are printed in the runserver terminal instead.
# Use a Gmail account with 2-Step Verification on, and an app password from
# https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords (not your normal Gmail password).
# EMAIL_HOST_USER=yourname@gmail.com
# EMAIL_HOST_PASSWORD=abcdefghijklmnop

# Another provider: also set its server. Port 587 uses STARTTLS, port 465 SSL.
# EMAIL_HOST=smtp.example.com
# EMAIL_PORT=587

# Set to 0 to stop all appointment emails.
# EMAIL_NOTIFICATIONS=1

# ---- Only on the server (see DEPLOY.md) -------------------------------------
# DJANGO_DEBUG=0
# DJANGO_SECRET_KEY=a long random value, made with: python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(50))"
# DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS=your-elastic-ip,localhost,127.0.0.1
